+A visit is booked against a particular pet and carries the date it is for and a short description of what it is for `[REQ-VIS-001]`. When booking, the pet's earlier visits are shown alongside, so whoever is booking can see what has already been done `[REQ-VIS-002]`. A visit is sometimes booked against the wrong pet or for the wrong day, so an upcoming visit — one dated later than today — can be cancelled from the owner's record, which removes it from that pet's record; the owner's record offers a cancel action beside each upcoming visit `[REQ-VIS-003]`. A visit whose date has passed cannot be cancelled, so the record of what has already happened is never altered.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a pet, when a description and a date later than today are supplied, then the visit is recorded and the booking is confirmed.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a blank description, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the description is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a date of today or earlier, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the date is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-002]` given a pet with earlier visits, when a new visit is being booked, then those earlier visits are shown with their dates and descriptions.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given an owner's record with a pet that has an upcoming visit, when the record is shown, then a cancel action is offered beside that visit.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a pet's upcoming visit, when it is cancelled from the owner's record, then the visit no longer appears on that pet's record and the owner's record is shown again.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a visit dated today or earlier, when the owner's record is shown, then no cancel action is offered beside that visit.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a cancel request naming a visit that does not belong to the named owner's pet, when it is submitted, then it is refused and nothing is removed.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. Booking a visit for a pet that does not belong to the named owner is refused.
 2. The date offered by default is the earliest date that would be accepted.
+3. Only an upcoming visit — one dated later than today, the same boundary booking enforces — can be cancelled; a visit whose date has passed is immutable.
+4. Cancelling one of a pet's visits leaves the pet's other visits in place.
+
+**ADR:** [ADR: Visit Cancellation as a Hard Delete](adr/2026-08-05-visit-cancellation-as-hard-delete.md)  ·  **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
